/-!
# The house of an algebraic number

The *house* `⌈x⌉` of an element `x` of a field of characteristic zero is the largest absolute
value of a complex root of `minpoly ℚ x`, that is, the largest modulus of a complex conjugate of
`x`. The value at a transcendental element is `0`.

Mathlib's `NumberField.house` is the same quantity for an element of a fixed number field, computed
through its complex embeddings. The version here needs neither a number field nor a complex
embedding of the ambient field: only `minpoly ℚ x` is mapped to `ℂ`. It is therefore constant on
conjugacy classes and invariant under field embeddings, and it agrees with `NumberField.house` on
number fields (`TauCeti.house_eq_numberField_house`). The sub-multiplicativity and
sub-additivity of the house for algebraic elements are obtained by computing in the number field
generated by the elements involved.

Together with the naive height and the Mahler measure, the house controls the size of the
conjugates of an algebraic number. It enters Liouville-type lower bounds, the bound of the naive
height of an algebraic integer by a power of its house, and the finiteness of algebraic integers
of bounded degree and bounded house.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.house x`: the largest modulus of a complex root of `minpoly ℚ x`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.norm_le_house_of_mem_rootSet`, `TauCeti.house_le_iff`,
  `TauCeti.exists_mem_rootSet_norm_eq_house`: the house is the maximum of the moduli of the
  complex conjugates; in particular `‖x‖ ≤ ⌈x⌉` for algebraic `x ∈ ℂ` (`TauCeti.norm_le_house`).
* `TauCeti.house_eq_numberField_house`: on a number field the house is `NumberField.house`.
* `TauCeti.house_map`, `TauCeti.house_eq_of_minpoly_eq`: invariance under field embeddings and
  conjugation.
* `TauCeti.house_mul_le`, `TauCeti.house_add_le`, `TauCeti.house_pow`: the house is
  sub-multiplicative, sub-additive and multiplicative on powers.
* `TauCeti.one_le_house`, `TauCeti.house_eq_one_iff`: a nonzero algebraic integer has house at
  least `1`, and Kronecker's theorem, an algebraic integer has house `1` exactly when it is a root
  of unity.
* `TauCeti.exists_algEquiv_one_le_norm`: a nonzero algebraic integer of a finite normal subfield
  `L` of `ℂ` has a Galois conjugate over `ℚ` of modulus at least `1`.
* `TauCeti.house_le_mahlerMeasure`,
  `TauCeti.mahlerMeasure_le_leadingCoeff_mul_max_one_house_pow`: the comparisons
  `⌈x⌉ ≤ M(x) ≤ a₀ max(1, ⌈x⌉)ᵈ` with the Mahler measure.
* `TauCeti.naiveHeight_le_two_mul_pow_of_house_le`, `TauCeti.naiveHeight_le_two_mul_house_pow`:
  an algebraic integer of degree `d` has naive height at most `(2B)ᵈ` whenever its house is at
  most `B` with `1 ≤ B`; in particular a nonzero algebraic integer satisfies
  `H(x) ≤ (2 ⌈x⌉)ᵈ`.
* `TauCeti.exists_numberField_of_isIntegral_natCast_mul`: an element `α` with `b α` integral
  lies in the number field `ℚ(α)` of degree `deg α`, with the same house.
* `NumberField.house_natCast_mul_pow_mul_pow_le`: the house of `c bⁿ αʲ` in a number field is
  at most `(2 b max(1, ⌈α⌉))ⁿ` when `c ≤ 2ⁿ` and `j ≤ n`.
* `NumberField.one_le_norm_mul_house_pow`: Liouville's inequality, a nonzero algebraic integer
  `x` of a number field of degree `d` satisfies `1 ≤ ‖σ x‖ ⌈x⌉ᵈ⁻¹` for every complex embedding
  `σ`.
* `NumberField.eq_zero_of_norm_le_exp_of_house_le_exp`: Liouville's inequality in exponential
  form, an element `y` of a number field with `m ^ N y` integral is zero once `‖σ y‖`, `⌈y⌉` and
  `|m| ^ N` are small enough.
* `TauCeti.inv_norm_le_pow_mul_house_pow_of_mem_rootSet`,
  `TauCeti.inv_norm_le_natDenominator_pow_mul_house_pow_of_mem_rootSet`,
  `TauCeti.inv_norm_le_natDenominator_pow_mul_house_pow`: every complex conjugate `z` of a
  nonzero algebraic number `x` of degree `d` satisfies `‖z‖ ≥ den(x)⁻ᵈ ⌈x⌉¹⁻ᵈ`, and more
  generally `‖z‖ ≥ b⁻ᵈ ⌈x⌉¹⁻ᵈ` whenever `b x` is integral for some positive integer `b`.

## References

* J.-H. Evertse, *Diophantine Approximation*, lecture notes (2019), ch. 3, §3.4 and
  Exercises 3.5, 3.6; ch. 3, Lemma 3.6, p. 42, for the Galois conjugate of modulus at least `1`;
  ch. 3, Exercise 3.7, p. 60, for the lower bound `‖z‖ ≥ den(z)⁻ᵈ ⌈z⌉¹⁻ᵈ`.
* C. Smyth, *The Mahler measure of algebraic numbers: a survey* (2008), §3.
-/

public section

open Polynomial

open scoped IntermediateField

namespace TauCeti

variable {F : Type*} [Field F] [CharZero F] {F' : Type*} [Field F'] [CharZero F']

/-- The *house* `⌈x⌉` of `x`: the largest modulus of a complex root of `minpoly ℚ x`, that is,
of a complex conjugate of `x`. For transcendental `x` the minimal polynomial is `0`, it has no
roots, and the house is `0`. -/
noncomputable def house (x : F) : ℝ :=
  ⨆ z : (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ, ‖(z : ℂ)‖

/-- The house of `x` is the supremum of the moduli of the complex roots of `minpoly ℚ x`. -/
theorem house_def (x : F) : house x = ⨆ z : (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ, ‖(z : ℂ)‖ := (rfl)

/-- The house is nonnegative. -/
theorem house_nonneg (x : F) : 0 ≤ house x :=
  Real.iSup_nonneg fun _ ↦ norm_nonneg _

/-- Every complex conjugate of `x` has modulus at most the house of `x`. -/
theorem norm_le_house_of_mem_rootSet {x : F} {z : ℂ} (hz : z ∈ (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ) :
    ‖z‖ ≤ house x :=
  le_ciSup (f := fun z : (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ ↦ ‖(z : ℂ)‖) (Set.finite_range _).bddAbove
    ⟨z, hz⟩

/-- An algebraic complex number has modulus at most its house. -/
theorem norm_le_house {x : ℂ} (hx : IsAlgebraic ℚ x) : ‖x‖ ≤ house x :=
  norm_le_house_of_mem_rootSet <|
    (mem_rootSet_of_ne (minpoly.ne_zero hx.isIntegral)).2 (minpoly.aeval ℚ x)

/-- For `C ≥ 0`, the house of `x` is at most `C` exactly when every complex conjugate of `x` has
modulus at most `C`. -/
theorem house_le_iff {x : F} {C : ℝ} (hC : 0 ≤ C) :
    house x ≤ C ↔ ∀ z ∈ (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ, ‖z‖ ≤ C :=
  ⟨fun h _ hz ↦ (norm_le_house_of_mem_rootSet hz).trans h,
    fun h ↦ Real.iSup_le (fun z ↦ h z z.2) hC⟩

/-- The house of an algebraic element is attained: it is the modulus of some complex conjugate. -/
theorem exists_mem_rootSet_norm_eq_house {x : F} (hx : IsAlgebraic ℚ x) :
    ∃ z ∈ (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ, ‖z‖ = house x := by
  have hint := hx.isIntegral
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := IsAlgClosed.exists_aeval_eq_zero ℂ (minpoly ℚ x) (minpoly.degree_pos hint).ne'
  have : Nonempty ((minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ) :=
    ⟨⟨z, (mem_rootSet_of_ne (minpoly.ne_zero hint)).2 hz⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := exists_eq_ciSup_of_finite (f := fun z : (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ ↦ ‖(z : ℂ)‖)
  exact ⟨w, w.2, hw⟩

/-- On a number field, the house is Mathlib's `NumberField.house`: the largest modulus of the
image of `x` under a complex embedding. -/
theorem house_eq_numberField_house {K : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K] (x : K) :
    house x = NumberField.house x := by
  have hroots := NumberField.Embeddings.range_eval_eq_rootSet_minpoly K ℂ x
  refine le_antisymm ((house_le_iff (NumberField.house_nonneg x)).2 fun z hz ↦ ?_) ?_
  · obtain ⟨φ, rfl⟩ := hroots.symm.subset hz
    exact NumberField.norm_embedding_le_house x φ
  · obtain ⟨φ, -, hφ⟩ := Finset.exists_mem_eq_sup' Finset.univ_nonempty fun φ : K →+* ℂ ↦ ‖φ x‖₊
    rw [NumberField.house_eq_sup', hφ, coe_nnnorm]
    exact norm_le_house_of_mem_rootSet (hroots ▸ ⟨φ, rfl⟩)

open Height NumberField in
/-- Every conjugate of a number-field element has modulus at most the exponential of its
relative logarithmic height. -/
theorem _root_.NumberField.house_le_exp_logHeight₁ {K : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K]
    (x : K) : NumberField.house x ≤ Real.exp (logHeight₁ x) := by
  by_cases hx : x = 0
  · simp [hx, NumberField.house]
  rw [NumberField.house, canonicalEmbedding]
  refine (pi_norm_le_iff_of_nonneg (Real.exp_pos _).le).mpr fun φ ↦ ?_
  let w : InfinitePlace K := InfinitePlace.mk φ
  have h := TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.abs_log_normalizedAbsValue_le_logHeight₁
    (Sum.inr w) x
  simp only [TauCeti.GlobalNumberFields.normalizedAbsValue_inr, Real.log_pow, abs_mul,
    Nat.abs_cast] at h
  have hm : (1 : ℝ) ≤ w.mult := by exact_mod_cast InfinitePlace.mult_pos (w := w)
  have hw : Real.log (w x) ≤ logHeight₁ x :=
    (le_abs_self _).trans ((le_mul_of_one_le_left (abs_nonneg _) hm).trans h)
  -- The place constructed from φ evaluates x as the complex norm of φ x.
  change w x ≤ Real.exp (logHeight₁ x)
  rw [← Real.exp_log (InfinitePlace.pos_iff.mpr hx)]
  exact Real.exp_le_exp.mpr hw

/-- The house depends only on `minpoly ℚ x`: conjugates, possibly lying in different fields, have
equal house. -/
theorem house_eq_of_minpoly_eq {x : F} {y : F'} (h : minpoly ℚ x = minpoly ℚ y) :
    house x = house y := by
  rw [house_def, house_def, h]

/-- Field embeddings preserve the house. -/
@[simp]
theorem house_map (f : F →+* F') (x : F) : house (f x) = house x :=
  house_eq_of_minpoly_eq (minpoly.algHom_eq f.toRatAlgHom f.injective x)

/-- Transcendental elements have house `0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem house_of_not_isAlgebraic {x : F} (hx : ¬IsAlgebraic ℚ x) : house x = 0 := by
  rw [house_def, minpoly.eq_zero (isAlgebraic_iff_isIntegral.not.mp hx), rootSet_zero]
  exact Real.iSup_of_isEmpty _

/-- The house of an element of a number field inside `F` is computed in that number field. -/
private lemma house_coe {K : IntermediateField ℚ F} [NumberField K] (a : K) :
    house (a : F) = NumberField.house a := by
  rw [← IntermediateField.algebraMap_apply, house_map, house_eq_numberField_house]

/-- The house of a rational number is its absolute value, independently of the field containing
it. -/
@[simp]
theorem house_ratCast (q : ℚ) : house (q : F) = |(q : ℝ)| := by
  have hroots : (minpoly ℚ (q : F)).rootSet ℂ = {(q : ℂ)} := by
    rw [← eq_ratCast (algebraMap ℚ F), minpoly.eq_X_sub_C]
    ext z
    simp [mem_rootSet_of_ne (X_sub_C_ne_zero _), sub_eq_zero]
  rw [house_def, hroots]
  simp

/-- The house of an integer is its absolute value. -/
@[simp]
theorem house_intCast (n : ℤ) : house (n : F) = |(n : ℝ)| := by
  simpa using house_ratCast (F := F) n

/-- The house of a natural number is itself. -/
@[simp]
theorem house_natCast (n : ℕ) : house (n : F) = n := by
  simpa using house_ratCast (F := F) n

/-- The house of `0` is `0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem house_zero : house (0 : F) = 0 := by
  simpa using house_natCast (F := F) 0

/-- The house of `1` is `1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem house_one : house (1 : F) = 1 := by
  simpa using house_natCast (F := F) 1

/-- The house of a product of algebraic elements is at most the product of their houses. -/
theorem house_mul_le {x y : F} (hx : IsAlgebraic ℚ x) (hy : IsAlgebraic ℚ y) :
    house (x * y) ≤ house x * house y := by
  obtain ⟨K, _, a, b, rfl, rfl⟩ := exists_numberField_mem hx hy
  rw [← IntermediateField.coe_mul, house_coe, house_coe, house_coe]
  exact NumberField.house_mul_le a b

/-- The house of a sum of algebraic elements is at most the sum of their houses. -/
theorem house_add_le {x y : F} (hx : IsAlgebraic ℚ x) (hy : IsAlgebraic ℚ y) :
    house (x + y) ≤ house x + house y := by
  obtain ⟨K, _, a, b, rfl, rfl⟩ := exists_numberField_mem hx hy
  rw [← IntermediateField.coe_add, house_coe, house_coe, house_coe]
  exact NumberField.house_add_le a b

/-- The house is multiplicative on powers. For transcendental `x` and `n ≠ 0` both sides are
`0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem house_pow (x : F) (n : ℕ) : house (x ^ n) = house x ^ n := by
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with rfl | hn
  · simp
  by_cases hx : IsAlgebraic ℚ x
  · obtain ⟨K, _, a, -, rfl, -⟩ := exists_numberField_mem hx hx
    rw [← IntermediateField.coe_pow, house_coe, house_coe, NumberField.house_pow]
  · rw [house_of_not_isAlgebraic hx, house_of_not_isAlgebraic fun h ↦ hx (h.of_pow hn),
      zero_pow hn.ne']

/-- A nonzero algebraic integer has house at least `1`. -/
theorem one_le_house {x : F} (hx : IsIntegral ℤ x) (h0 : x ≠ 0) : 1 ≤ house x := by
  have halg : IsAlgebraic ℚ x := (hx.tower_top (A := ℚ)).isAlgebraic
  obtain ⟨K, _, a, -, rfl, -⟩ := exists_numberField_mem halg halg
  rw [house_coe]
  rw [← IntermediateField.algebraMap_apply, isIntegral_algebraMap_iff] at hx
  exact NumberField.one_le_house_of_isIntegral hx (by simpa using h0)

/-- **A Galois conjugate of modulus at least `1`.** A nonzero algebraic integer `x` of a finite
normal subfield `L` of `ℂ` has a Galois conjugate `τ x`, for some `τ ∈ Gal(L/ℚ)`, of modulus at
least `1`. This is the form of `NumberField.exists_conjugate_one_le_norm` for a field embedded in
`ℂ`, with its complex embeddings replaced by its automorphisms. -/
theorem exists_algEquiv_one_le_norm {L : IntermediateField ℚ ℂ} [FiniteDimensional ℚ L]
    [Normal ℚ L] {x : L} (hx : IsIntegral ℤ x) (h0 : x ≠ 0) :
    ∃ τ : Gal(L/ℚ), 1 ≤ ‖((τ x : L) : ℂ)‖ := by
  have : NumberField L := ⟨⟩
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := NumberField.exists_conjugate_one_le_norm (α := ⟨x, hx⟩)
    fun h ↦ h0 congr($h.1)
  refine ⟨σ.toRatAlgHom.restrictNormal' L, ?_⟩
  -- `σ` restricted to the normal field `L` and followed by the inclusion is `σ` again.
  have hτ := σ.toRatAlgHom.restrictNormal_commutes L x
  rw [Algebra.algebraMap_self, RingHom.id_apply] at hτ
  rw [AlgHom.restrictNormal', AlgEquiv.ofBijective_apply, ← IntermediateField.algebraMap_apply,
    hτ]
  exact hσ

/-- **Kronecker's theorem.** An algebraic integer has house `1` exactly when it is a root of
unity. -/
theorem house_eq_one_iff {x : F} (hx : IsIntegral ℤ x) :
    house x = 1 ↔ ∃ n : ℕ, 0 < n ∧ x ^ n = 1 := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun ⟨n, hn, hxn⟩ ↦ ?_⟩
  · have h0 : x ≠ 0 := by
      rintro rfl
      simp at h
    have halg : IsAlgebraic ℚ x := (hx.tower_top (A := ℚ)).isAlgebraic
    obtain ⟨K, _, a, -, rfl, -⟩ := exists_numberField_mem halg halg
    rw [house_coe] at h
    rw [← IntermediateField.algebraMap_apply, isIntegral_algebraMap_iff] at hx
    obtain ⟨n, hn, han⟩ := NumberField.Embeddings.pow_eq_one_of_norm_le_one K ℂ
      (by simpa using h0) hx fun φ ↦ (NumberField.norm_embedding_le_house a φ).trans h.le
    exact ⟨n, hn, by rw [← IntermediateField.coe_pow, han, IntermediateField.coe_one]⟩
  · have h := house_pow x n
    rw [hxn, house_one] at h
    exact ((pow_eq_one_iff_of_nonneg (house_nonneg x) hn.ne').mp h.symm)

/-- The house is at most the Mahler measure. For an algebraic `x` the largest conjugate modulus
`|z|` is bounded by its factor `max(1, |z|)` of `M(x) = a₀ ∏ max(1, |z|)`, and the other factors
are at least `1`; for transcendental `x` this reads `0 ≤ 1`. -/
theorem house_le_mahlerMeasure (x : F) : house x ≤ mahlerMeasure x := by
  refine (house_le_iff (zero_le_one.trans (one_le_mahlerMeasure x))).2 fun z hz ↦ ?_
  have hz' : z ∈ (minpoly ℚ x).aroots ℂ := mem_aroots'.2 (mem_rootSet'.1 hz)
  have ha₀ : (1 : ℝ) ≤ (primitiveMinpoly x).leadingCoeff := by
    exact_mod_cast (leadingCoeff_primitiveMinpoly_pos x)
  have h := Multiset.mem_le_prod_of_one_le (fun w : ℂ ↦ le_max_left 1 ‖w‖) hz'
  rw [mahlerMeasure_eq_leadingCoeff_mul_prod]
  exact ((le_max_right 1 ‖z‖).trans h).trans
    (le_mul_of_one_le_left (zero_le_one.trans ((le_max_left 1 ‖z‖).trans h)) ha₀)

/-- The Mahler measure is at most `a₀ max(1, ⌈x⌉)ᵈ`, where `a₀` is the leading coefficient of the
primitive minimal polynomial and `d` the degree of `x`. -/
theorem mahlerMeasure_le_leadingCoeff_mul_max_one_house_pow (x : F) :
    mahlerMeasure x ≤
      (primitiveMinpoly x).leadingCoeff * max 1 (house x) ^ (minpoly ℚ x).natDegree := by
  have ha₀ : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (primitiveMinpoly x).leadingCoeff := by
    exact_mod_cast (leadingCoeff_primitiveMinpoly_pos x).le
  rw [mahlerMeasure_eq_leadingCoeff_mul_prod, ← IsAlgClosed.card_aroots_eq_natDegree (B := ℂ),
    ← Multiset.prod_replicate, ← Multiset.map_const']
  gcongr
  refine Multiset.prod_map_le_prod_map₀ _ _ (fun _ _ ↦ by positivity) fun z hz ↦ ?_
  gcongr
  exact norm_le_house_of_mem_rootSet (mem_rootSet'.2 (mem_aroots'.1 hz))

/-- An algebraic integer of degree `d` whose house is at most `B`, with `1 ≤ B`, has naive height
at most `(2B)ᵈ`. -/
theorem naiveHeight_le_two_mul_pow_of_house_le {x : F} (hx : IsIntegral ℤ x) {B : ℝ}
    (hB : 1 ≤ B) (hxB : house x ≤ B) :
    naiveHeight x ≤ (2 * B) ^ (minpoly ℚ x).natDegree := by
  have halg : IsAlgebraic ℚ x := (hx.tower_top (A := ℚ)).isAlgebraic
  have hmon : (primitiveMinpoly x).Monic := by
    rw [primitiveMinpoly_eq_minpoly_int hx]
    exact minpoly.monic hx
  -- The roots of `F_x` in `ℂ` are the conjugates of `x`, so the coefficients of the monic `F_x`,
  -- elementary symmetric functions of them, satisfy `|aᵢ| ≤ binom(d, i) Bᵈ⁻ⁱ ≤ 2ᵈ Bᵈ`.
  have hroots : ∀ z ∈ ((primitiveMinpoly x).map (Int.castRingHom ℂ)).roots, ‖z‖ ≤ B := by
    intro z hz
    refine (norm_le_house_of_mem_rootSet ?_).trans hxB
    rw [← rootSet_primitiveMinpoly halg, rootSet_def, Finset.mem_coe, Multiset.mem_toFinset,
      aroots_def, algebraMap_int_eq]
    exact hz
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := (primitiveMinpoly x).exists_eq_supNorm
  rw [naiveHeight_def, hi, ← natDegree_primitiveMinpoly]
  have hcoeff := coeff_le_of_roots_le i hmon (IsAlgClosed.splits _) hroots
  rw [coeff_map, eq_intCast, Complex.norm_intCast, ← Int.norm_eq_abs] at hcoeff
  set n := (primitiveMinpoly x).natDegree
  calc ‖(primitiveMinpoly x).coeff i‖ ≤ B ^ (n - i) * n.choose i := hcoeff
    _ ≤ B ^ n * 2 ^ n := by
        gcongr
        · exact Nat.sub_le n i
        · exact_mod_cast Nat.choose_le_two_pow n i
    _ = (2 * B) ^ n := by rw [mul_pow, mul_comm]

/-- A nonzero algebraic integer `x` of degree `d` has naive height at most `(2 ⌈x⌉)ᵈ`. -/
theorem naiveHeight_le_two_mul_house_pow {x : F} (hx : IsIntegral ℤ x) (h0 : x ≠ 0) :
    naiveHeight x ≤ (2 * house x) ^ (minpoly ℚ x).natDegree :=
  naiveHeight_le_two_mul_pow_of_house_le hx (one_le_house hx h0) le_rfl

/-- An element `α` of `F` such that `b α` is integral over `ℤ` for some `b ≠ 0` lies in an
intermediate number field `K` of degree `deg α`, namely `ℚ(α)`: there is `α' ∈ K` mapping to
`α` such that `b α'` is integral and `house α' = house α`. This reduces the construction of
auxiliary polynomials for such `α` to Siegel's lemma over a number field. -/
theorem exists_numberField_of_isIntegral_natCast_mul {α : F} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ≠ 0)
    (hbα : IsIntegral ℤ ((b : F) * α)) :
    ∃ (K : IntermediateField ℚ F) (_ : NumberField K) (α' : K), algebraMap K F α' = α ∧
      Module.finrank ℚ K = (minpoly ℚ α).natDegree ∧ IsIntegral ℤ ((b : K) * α') ∧
      NumberField.house α' = house α := by
  have hα := isIntegral_rat_of_isIntegral_natCast_mul hb hbα
  have : FiniteDimensional ℚ ℚ⟮α⟯ := IntermediateField.adjoin.finiteDimensional hα
  have : NumberField ℚ⟮α⟯ := {}
  have hα' := IntermediateField.AdjoinSimple.algebraMap_gen ℚ α
  refine ⟨ℚ⟮α⟯, this, IntermediateField.AdjoinSimple.gen ℚ α, hα',
    IntermediateField.adjoin.finrank hα, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [← isIntegral_algHom_iff ((IsScalarTower.toAlgHom ℚ ℚ⟮α⟯ F).restrictScalars ℤ)
      (algebraMap ℚ⟮α⟯ F).injective]
    simpa [IntermediateField.AdjoinSimple.coe_gen] using hbα
  · rw [← house_coe, ← IntermediateField.algebraMap_apply, hα']

/-- **Liouville's inequality** in a number field `K` of degree `d`: a nonzero algebraic integer
`x ∈ K` satisfies `1 ≤ ‖σ x‖ ⌈x⌉ᵈ⁻¹` for every embedding `σ : K →+* ℂ`, since its norm is a
nonzero integer. -/
theorem _root_.NumberField.one_le_norm_mul_house_pow {K : Type*} [Field K] [NumberField K]
    {x : K} (hx : IsIntegral ℤ x) (h0 : x ≠ 0) (σ : K →+* ℂ) :
    1 ≤ ‖σ x‖ * NumberField.house x ^ (Module.finrank ℚ K - 1) := by
  have h1 : (1 : ℝ) ≤ |(Algebra.norm ℚ x : ℝ)| :=
    NumberField.RingOfIntegers.one_le_abs_norm (α := ⟨x, hx⟩) fun h ↦ h0 (congr_arg Subtype.val h)
  rw [← Real.norm_eq_abs, Rat.norm_cast_real] at h1
  exact h1.trans (NumberField.norm_norm_le_norm_mul_house_pow x σ)

/-- **Liouville's inequality in exponential form.** Let `K` be a number field of degree `d`,
`σ : K →+* ℂ`, `y ∈ K` and `m ≠ 0` an integer with `m ^ N y` an algebraic integer. If
`‖σ y‖ ≤ exp A`, `⌈y⌉ ≤ exp B` and `|m| ^ N ≤ exp C` with `C + A + (d - 1) (C + B) < 0`,
then `y = 0`. -/
theorem _root_.NumberField.eq_zero_of_norm_le_exp_of_house_le_exp {K : Type*} [Field K]
    [NumberField K] (σ : K →+* ℂ) {y : K} {m : ℤ} (hm : m ≠ 0) {N : ℕ}
    (hint : IsIntegral ℤ ((m : K) ^ N * y)) {A B C : ℝ} (hσ : ‖σ y‖ ≤ Real.exp A)
    (hy : NumberField.house y ≤ Real.exp B) (hmC : |(m : ℝ)| ^ N ≤ Real.exp C)
    (h : C + A + (Module.finrank ℚ K - 1 : ℕ) * (C + B) < 0) :
    y = 0 := by
  by_contra hy0
  have hx0 : (m : K) ^ N * y ≠ 0 := mul_ne_zero (pow_ne_zero _ (Int.cast_ne_zero.2 hm)) hy0
  have hσx : ‖σ ((m : K) ^ N * y)‖ ≤ Real.exp C * Real.exp A := by
    rw [map_mul, map_pow, map_intCast, norm_mul, norm_pow, Complex.norm_intCast]
    exact mul_le_mul hmC hσ (norm_nonneg _) (Real.exp_pos _).le
  have hhx : NumberField.house ((m : K) ^ N * y) ≤ Real.exp C * Real.exp B := by
    refine (NumberField.house_mul_le _ _).trans
      (mul_le_mul ?_ hy (NumberField.house_nonneg _) (Real.exp_pos _).le)
    rwa [NumberField.house_pow, NumberField.house_intCast, Int.cast_abs]
  have hlt :
      Real.exp C * Real.exp A * (Real.exp C * Real.exp B) ^ (Module.finrank ℚ K - 1) < 1 := by
    rw [← Real.exp_add, ← Real.exp_add, ← Real.exp_nat_mul, ← Real.exp_add]
    exact Real.exp_lt_one_iff.2 (by linarith)
  refine absurd (lt_of_le_of_lt ?_ hlt) (lt_irrefl 1)
  exact (NumberField.one_le_norm_mul_house_pow hint hx0 σ).trans <| mul_le_mul hσx
    (pow_le_pow_left₀ (NumberField.house_nonneg _) hhx _)
    (pow_nonneg (NumberField.house_nonneg _) _) (by positivity)

/-- A Liouville-type lower bound for the conjugates of a nonzero algebraic number: if `b ≠ 0`
and `b x` is integral over `ℤ`, then every complex conjugate `z` of `x` satisfies
`‖z‖⁻¹ ≤ bᵈ ⌈x⌉ᵈ⁻¹`, that is, `‖z‖ ≥ b⁻ᵈ ⌈x⌉¹⁻ᵈ`, where `d` is the degree of `x`. For an
algebraic integer `x` one may take `b = 1`. -/
theorem inv_norm_le_pow_mul_house_pow_of_mem_rootSet {x : F} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ≠ 0)
    (hbx : IsIntegral ℤ ((b : F) * x)) (h0 : x ≠ 0) {z : ℂ}
    (hz : z ∈ (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ) :
    ‖z‖⁻¹ ≤ (b : ℝ) ^ (minpoly ℚ x).natDegree * house x ^ ((minpoly ℚ x).natDegree - 1) := by
  obtain ⟨K, _, α, rfl, hfin, hint, hhouse⟩ := exists_numberField_of_isIntegral_natCast_mul hb hbx
  have hα0 : α ≠ 0 := by rintro rfl; simp at h0
  have hmin : minpoly ℚ (algebraMap K F α) = minpoly ℚ α :=
    minpoly.algHom_eq (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom ℚ K F) (algebraMap K F).injective α
  rw [hmin] at hz
  obtain ⟨σ, rfl⟩ : ∃ σ : K →+* ℂ, σ α = z := by
    rwa [← NumberField.Embeddings.range_eval_eq_rootSet_minpoly] at hz
  -- Liouville's inequality for the nonzero algebraic integer `b α`, whose conjugates have modulus
  -- at most `b ⌈x⌉`.
  have hnorm := NumberField.one_le_norm_mul_house_pow hint
    (mul_ne_zero (Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr hb) hα0) σ
  rw [NumberField.house_nat_mul, hhouse, hfin, hmin] at hnorm
  have hd : (minpoly ℚ α).natDegree = (minpoly ℚ α).natDegree - 1 + 1 :=
    (Nat.sub_add_cancel (minpoly.natDegree_pos (Algebra.IsIntegral.isIntegral α))).symm
  have hσ : 0 < ‖σ α‖ := norm_pos_iff.mpr ((map_ne_zero σ).mpr hα0)
  rw [hmin, inv_le_iff_one_le_mul₀' hσ]
  calc (1 : ℝ)
      ≤ b * ‖σ α‖ * (b * house (algebraMap K F α)) ^ ((minpoly ℚ α).natDegree - 1) := by
        simpa using hnorm
    _ = _ := by rw [hd, pow_succ, Nat.add_sub_cancel]; ring

/-- The lower bound `‖z‖⁻¹ ≤ den(x)ᵈ ⌈x⌉ᵈ⁻¹` for every complex conjugate `z` of a nonzero
algebraic number `x` of degree `d`, where `den(x)` is its natural-number denominator.
Equivalently, `‖z‖ ≥ den(x)⁻ᵈ ⌈x⌉¹⁻ᵈ`. -/
theorem inv_norm_le_natDenominator_pow_mul_house_pow_of_mem_rootSet {x : F} (h0 : x ≠ 0)
    {z : ℂ} (hz : z ∈ (minpoly ℚ x).rootSet ℂ) :
    ‖z‖⁻¹ ≤ (Algebra.natDenominator x : ℝ) ^ (minpoly ℚ x).natDegree *
      house x ^ ((minpoly ℚ x).natDegree - 1) := by
  have hx : IsAlgebraic ℚ x := by
    by_contra hx
    simp [minpoly.eq_zero (fun h ↦ hx h.isAlgebraic)] at hz
  refine inv_norm_le_pow_mul_house_pow_of_mem_rootSet
    (IsAlgebraic.natDenominator_ne_zero ((IsFractionRing.isAlgebraic_iff ℤ ℚ F).2 hx)) ?_ h0 hz
  simpa [nsmul_eq_mul] using Algebra.isIntegral_natDenominator_smul x

/-- A nonzero algebraic complex number `z` of degree `d` satisfies
`‖z‖⁻¹ ≤ den(z)ᵈ ⌈z⌉ᵈ⁻¹`, that is, `‖z‖ ≥ den(z)⁻ᵈ ⌈z⌉¹⁻ᵈ`. -/
theorem inv_norm_le_natDenominator_pow_mul_house_pow {z : ℂ} (hz : IsAlgebraic ℚ z)
    (h0 : z ≠ 0) :
    ‖z‖⁻¹ ≤ (Algebra.natDenominator z : ℝ) ^ (minpoly ℚ z).natDegree *
      house z ^ ((minpoly ℚ z).natDegree - 1) :=
  inv_norm_le_natDenominator_pow_mul_house_pow_of_mem_rootSet h0 <|
    (mem_rootSet_of_ne (minpoly.ne_zero hz.isIntegral)).2 (minpoly.aeval ℚ z)

/-- In a number field, the house of `c b ^ n α ^ j` is at most `(2 b max(1, ⌈α⌉)) ^ n` when
`c ≤ 2 ^ n` and `j ≤ n`. -/
theorem _root_.NumberField.house_natCast_mul_pow_mul_pow_le {K : Type*} [Field K]
    [NumberField K] (α : K) {b c j n : ℕ} (hc : c ≤ 2 ^ n) (hj : j ≤ n) :
    NumberField.house ((c : K) * ((b : K) ^ n * α ^ j)) ≤
      (2 * b * max 1 (NumberField.house α)) ^ n := by
  have hα : NumberField.house α ^ j ≤ max 1 (NumberField.house α) ^ n :=
    (pow_le_pow_left₀ (NumberField.house_nonneg α) (le_max_right _ _) j).trans
      (pow_le_pow_right₀ (le_max_left _ _) hj)
  rw [← Nat.cast_pow, NumberField.house_nat_mul, NumberField.house_nat_mul,
    NumberField.house_pow, mul_pow, mul_pow, Nat.cast_pow, mul_assoc]
  exact mul_le_mul (by exact_mod_cast hc) (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hα (by positivity))
    (mul_nonneg (by positivity) (pow_nonneg (NumberField.house_nonneg α) j)) (by positivity)

/-! ### Examples -/

/- The house of `-2` is `2`. -/
example : house (-2 : ℂ) = 2 := by
  simpa using house_intCast (F := ℂ) (-2)

/- The house of `i` is `1`: it is an algebraic integer and a root of unity. -/
example : house Complex.I = 1 :=
  (house_eq_one_iff (Complex.isIntegral_I ℤ)).mpr ⟨4, by norm_num, Complex.I_pow_four⟩

/- On `ℚ`, the house agrees with Mathlib's number-field house. -/
example : house (2 : ℚ) = NumberField.house (2 : ℚ) :=
  house_eq_numberField_house 2

end TauCeti
